  "notes": [
    "Target is the first deployment 0xb7933eb7, the only migrator the anchor executed, created by 0x321fb100 at block 29462126 (0x10dbe4db), 28 hours before the anchor. The redeploy 0x839b0afd (block 29525530, same deployer and constructor arguments) differs only in sending refunds to params.recipient instead of msg.sender; it keeps the pull from params.recipient and the unchecked pair and tokens, so it is a sibling deployment of the same code and its drains are in the campaign (rule 4). Neither migrator is upgradeable. The victims' approvals are their own state and not a reset.",
    "Earliest exploit: every Migrate event of 0xb7933eb7 from its creation to the chain head (128 events) was checked for a recipient other than the transaction's sender or target. The first is the anchor (index 1 of block 29495770); 0xa8265823's own multicall 0xd090f307 (refs), at 3 gwei against the bot's 13.5, reverted at index 244. 75 such front-runs ran to block 29525576, each keeping the victim's refund: 54 by 0xf576c7f1 via 0x25f1424b, 13 by 0xcf09c0bc via 0xdad3f630, four by 0x1bbbbb0d, two by 0xf84efa8a and one each by 0xc4f82210 and 0xc50d1dcb. 0x740d618e's three fake-token migrations through 0x40a2accb (blocks 29566537-29601043) came after the redeploy's first.",
    "On the redeploy, all 626 transactions with a migrator event from its creation to block 32200000 were checked for LP that a party other than the transaction's sender or target sent to its pair for burning. The first is 0x706ea75c (0x1bc2bb87's LP, block 29552670); every earlier migration burned the sender's own LP. 86 transactions qualify, matching campaign.mjs's 86 exercises (it found three whose logs the BSC node attributes to neighbouring transactions): by 0xa1e31b29 (30), 0xa7a98876 (22, including the DeFiHackLabs transaction 0xebe52488), 0xe3aeede5 (17, among them the USDT/BUSD LP of 0xa68cc3d7 and 0x7f46134c, worth 332k and 362k) and four senders calling 0x6e11e90d with fake pair 0x73f3c0df (17 transactions, 103,332 USD, mostly 0x639ce846's 228 WBNB and 50,000 BUSD). Extending the event scan to the chain head (631 transactions) adds five more by that group (0xab62202a, 0x23f6b24a, 0x0b1ecabf, 0xb0a123cf, 0xcd2761cd; blocks 33263714-38761669, 1,669 USD), also in the campaign.",
    "Loss is the victims' depletion priced per transaction at DefiLlama (coingecko keys for USDT, BUSD, ETH, SHIB, SAND, NEAR and USDC, whose BSC keys return nothing). For the fake-token migrations (91 on the redeploy, three on the first deployment) it is the whole underlying of the burned LP (the pair's transfers to the migrator), 1,123,363 USD, since the victims received worthless fake-token positions that are not subtracted; for the 75 front-runs it is only the refunds the front-runners kept, 11,350 USD, since those victims still received their V3 positions. It is far above the 72k in DeFiHackLabs and DefiLlama, which cover only part of the first fake-token attackers' take."
